@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-application`

-- g1-tests-application.l4: tests of g1-application.l4 (s.5).  Group G1.
-- Expected values are decided from the text of s.5 as printed (inputs/law.wiki lines 78 to 81, checked on gazette page 183)
-- before any rule was run: the applicant is whoever seeks to obtain or to renew a licence; the licence application is the
-- application submitted to the Registrar; the Registrar may require information or a document he needs to decide the
-- application; he must publish the ways to apply and the list of documents.  The section states no period, so no deadline
-- is expected anywhere: a duty with no period stands until it is performed.

§ `Tests of s.5`

§§ `s.5(a) "applicant" and "licence application"`

`a person seeking a first licence` MEANS `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` WITH
    `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law` IS TRUE
    `seeks to renew a licence under the Law` IS FALSE
`a person seeking to renew` MEANS `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` WITH
    `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law` IS FALSE
    `seeks to renew a licence under the Law` IS TRUE
`a person seeking both` MEANS `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` WITH
    `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law` IS TRUE
    `seeks to renew a licence under the Law` IS TRUE
`a person seeking neither` MEANS `Facts about a person and a licence under section 5` WITH
    `seeks to obtain a licence under the Law` IS FALSE
    `seeks to renew a licence under the Law` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` `a person seeking a first licence`
#ASSERT `s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` `a person seeking to renew`
#ASSERT `s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` `a person seeking both`
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(a) — the person is an applicant` `a person seeking neither`

`a request to the Registrar by an applicant` MEANS `Facts about a request under section 5` WITH `submitted to the Registrar` IS TRUE, `submitted by an applicant` IS TRUE
`a request to the Registrar by a non-applicant` MEANS `Facts about a request under section 5` WITH `submitted to the Registrar` IS TRUE, `submitted by an applicant` IS FALSE
`a request to someone else by an applicant` MEANS `Facts about a request under section 5` WITH `submitted to the Registrar` IS FALSE, `submitted by an applicant` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `s 5(a) — the request is a licence application` `a request to the Registrar by an applicant`
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(a) — the request is a licence application` `a request to the Registrar by a non-applicant`
#ASSERT NOT `s 5(a) — the request is a licence application` `a request to someone else by an applicant`

§§ `s.5(a) the applicant must submit an application: no period is stated`

#TRACE `s 5(a) — the applicant must submit a licence application` `a person seeking a first licence` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `submit a licence application to the Registrar` AT 40
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
-- No period: the duty stands, however long the clock runs.
#TRACE `s 5(a) — the applicant must submit a licence application` `a person seeking a first licence` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 5(a) — the applicant must submit a licence application` `a person seeking to renew` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
-- A person who seeks neither licence has no duty to apply.
#TRACE `s 5(a) — the applicant must submit a licence application` `a person seeking neither` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED

§§ `s.5(b) the Registrar may require information or a document`

`a demand the Registrar needs` MEANS `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` WITH
    `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS TRUE
`a demand the Registrar does not need` MEANS `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` WITH
    `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS FALSE
`a demand made of a stranger` MEANS `Circumstances of a demand under section 5(b)` WITH
    `the demand is made of an applicant on a licence application` IS FALSE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the information or document is needed to decide the application` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the Registrar may require the information or document` `a demand the Registrar needs`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may require the information or document` `a demand the Registrar does not need`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may require the information or document` `a demand made of a stranger`

#TRACE `s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` `a demand the Registrar needs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `require information or a document from the applicant` AT 10
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
-- An unexercised permission with no period stands.
#TRACE `s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` `a demand the Registrar needs` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
-- Without need there is no permission.
#TRACE `s 5(b) — the Registrar may require information or a document` `a demand the Registrar does not need` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED

§§ `s.5(c) the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents to attach`

#TRACE `s 5(c) — the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents to attach` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Registrar` DOES `publish on the Ministry website how to apply for a licence and the documents to attach` AT 30
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
-- No period is stated: the duty stands, and is not a breach, however long it is left.
#TRACE `s 5(c) — the Registrar must publish how to apply and the documents to attach` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING
